{title: Paper Boats}
{artist: Linnea Vale}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[D]Folding paper b[G]oats from the morning news
[D]Sailing every headl[A]ine down the avenue
[D]Every gutter rive[G]r carries one away
[D]Out to where [A]the drains m[D]eet the bay
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]Paper boats, p[D]aper boats
[A]Somebody's going to [D]read you yet
[G]Paper boats, p[D]aper boats
[A]All the news we'd rat[D]her forget
{end_of_chorus}
